# Snapshot: working parallel Monte Carlo (1000 × 1000)

State as of 2026-05-20 13:23 EDT, after fixing two cross-worker collisions in
`run_montecarlo_parallel_slmode1_lunar.sh` + `run_montecarlo.sh`. This README
documents the exact recipe for the full 1000-trial × 1000-DL-first-TX sweep
across N workers on a single host.

## TL;DR

From repo root:

```bash
cd bictr_analysis

sudo -E ./run_montecarlo_parallel_slmode1_lunar.sh \
  --workers 4 \
  --trials 1000 \
  --target-tx 1000 \
  --warmup 15 \
  --duration 600 \
  2>&1 | tee "montecarlo_results/run_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)_parallel_1000x1000.log"
```

Increase `--workers` to whatever physical/logical cores you have (each worker
runs one `nr-softmodem` + one `nr-uesoftmodem` inside its own Linux network
namespace).

## What's working under the hood

Two collisions break multi-worker runs by default; both are now handled:

1. **TUN device name collision.** `nr-softmodem` hardcodes the TUN name
   `oaitun_enb1` in `openair1/SIMULATION/ETH_TRANSPORT/netlink_init.c` (`sprintf(ifname, "oaitun_%.3s%d", ifprefix, i+1)`).
   `nr-uesoftmodem` hardcodes `oaitun_ue1`. Both call `exit(1)` if the
   interface can't be created. With N>1 workers on one host, every worker
   after the first hits `EBUSY` and dies.

   **Fix**: each worker now runs inside its own `ip netns` (`mc_worker_<RUN_TAG>_<i>`).
   Per-netns interface namespace means `oaitun_enb1` / `oaitun_ue1` can exist
   N times without conflict.

2. **rfsim TCP port collision.** Default `rfsimulator.serverport = 4043` in
   every BICTR conf. With multiple workers, only the first binds.

   **Fix**: defense-in-depth — `run_montecarlo.sh` now sed-rewrites
   `serverport` in the per-trial `gnb.conf`/`ue.conf` from `OAI_RFSIM_PORT`,
   AND passes `--rfsimulator.[0].serverport` on the gNB CLI to defeat the
   array-element reset caused by `--rfsimulator.[0].serveraddr server`.
   In practice the netns isolation already protects each worker's `127.0.0.1:4043`,
   so the port arithmetic is belt-and-suspenders.

## Prerequisites

- OAI built at `cmake_targets/ran_build/build/{nr-softmodem,nr-uesoftmodem}`.
- `iproute2` (`ip` command) for netns. Already standard on Linux.
- `sudo` (the parallel script enforces `EUID == 0`).
- BICTR lunar DEM at `bictr_terrain/lunar_south_pole.bdem` (optional — OAI
  falls back to flat terrain if missing, with a warning).
- Optional but recommended: `pip3 install --user tqdm` for the live progress
  bar in the launching terminal.

## Recommended full command (with early-stop)

For a 1000 × 1000 campaign across all default MCS (0–28) and noise points
(11 values), strongly recommend enabling `--early-stop` so saturated cells
(BLER ≈ 0 at high SNR, BLER ≈ 1 at low SNR) skip the remaining 990+ trials:

```bash
sudo -E ./run_montecarlo_parallel_slmode1_lunar.sh \
  --workers 4 \
  --trials 1000 \
  --target-tx 1000 \
  --warmup 15 \
  --duration 600 \
  --early-stop 3 \
  2>&1 | tee "montecarlo_results/run_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)_parallel_1000x1000.log"
```

`--early-stop 3` is forwarded to `run_montecarlo.sh` and stops the trial loop
of a cell after 3 consecutive saturated or clean trials, reclaiming roughly
99% of the runtime for points off the waterfall edge.

## Banner sanity check at launch

You should see (port and netns names vary by run):

```
Worker 0: MCS {0,1,2,3,4,5,6}        build=.../worker_0  rfsim_port=4043  netns=mc_worker_<TAG>_0
Worker 1: MCS {7,8,9,10,11,12,13}    build=.../worker_1  rfsim_port=4044  netns=mc_worker_<TAG>_1
Worker 2: MCS {14,15,16,17,18,19,20} build=.../worker_2  rfsim_port=4045  netns=mc_worker_<TAG>_2
Worker 3: MCS {21,22,23,24,25,26,27,28} build=.../worker_3  rfsim_port=4046  netns=mc_worker_<TAG>_3
```

…followed by a `tqdm` bar (or `\rProgress: N/M trials (X%) workers finished K/4`
if `tqdm` isn't installed).

## Live monitoring

Aggregate (same terminal): the tqdm bar.

Per-worker:

```bash
RUN=$(ls -td montecarlo_results/parallel_slmode1_lunar_* | head -1)
tail -f "$RUN"/worker_*/worker.log
# or just one:
tail -f "$RUN/worker_0/worker.log"
```

What healthy progress looks like (all four workers ticking simultaneously):

```
[5/770] BICTR_LUNAR  MCS=0   noise_power_dB=6    trial=5 ... started (warmup 15s, target DL TX 1000, timeout 600s)
    progress: 10s, DL_first_tx=0/1000
    progress: 80s, DL_first_tx=565/1000
    progress: 90s, DL_first_tx=635/1000
DL_BLER=0.996183  UL_BLER=0.996183  DL_first_tx=1011 (target reached in 135s)
```

## One-shot health diagnostic (run any time)

```bash
RUN=$(ls -td montecarlo_results/parallel_slmode1_lunar_* | head -1)
TAG=$(basename "$RUN" | sed 's/^parallel_slmode1_lunar_//')
echo "RUN=$RUN"

echo "=== netns for this run (expect WORKERS many) ==="
sudo ip netns list | grep "mc_worker_${TAG}_" || echo "  NONE — patched script didn't run"

echo "=== per-netns: lo + oaitun_* up, one rfsim listener ==="
for ns in $(sudo ip netns list | awk -v t="mc_worker_${TAG}_" '$1 ~ t {print $1}'); do
  echo "--- $ns ---"
  sudo ip netns exec "$ns" ip -br link show | sed 's/^/    /'
  sudo ip netns exec "$ns" ss -ltn | awk 'NR==1 || $4 ~ /:404[0-9]$/' | sed 's/^/    /'
done

echo "=== OAI procs (8 main + their internal worker threads, so usually 8–16) ==="
ps -eo cmd | grep -E 'nr-(soft|uesoft)modem' | grep -v grep | wc -l

echo "=== nrMAC_stats.log per worker (all > 143 bytes, mtime recent) ==="
for d in montecarlo_parallel_builds_lunar/worker_*; do
  stat -c "%n  %s bytes  mtime=%y" "$d/nrMAC_stats.log"
done

echo "=== TUN EBUSY count in current tmp dirs (expect 0 each) ==="
for d in $(sudo ls -dt /tmp/mc_oai.* 2>/dev/null | head -n "$(ls -d montecarlo_parallel_builds_lunar/worker_* 2>/dev/null | wc -l)"); do
  printf "%s  gnb_ebusy=%s  ue_ebusy=%s\n" "$d" \
    "$(sudo grep -c 'Device or resource busy' "$d/gnb.log" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)" \
    "$(sudo grep -c 'Device or resource busy' "$d/ue.log"  2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
done
```

Pass criteria: netns count == workers, each netns shows `lo` UP plus
`oaitun_enb1` and `oaitun_ue1` UP plus a `:4043` listener; OAI procs ≥ 8;
all `nrMAC_stats.log` files > 143 bytes with recent mtimes; `gnb_ebusy` /
`ue_ebusy` == 0.

## Kill switch (if something goes sideways)

```bash
sudo pkill -f run_montecarlo_parallel_slmode1_lunar.sh
sudo pkill -f run_montecarlo.sh
sudo pkill -9 -f nr-softmodem
sudo pkill -9 -f nr-uesoftmodem
sudo rm -rf /tmp/mc_oai.*
sudo ip -all netns delete 2>/dev/null || true
```

The script's `trap cleanup_netns EXIT INT TERM` removes the `mc_worker_*`
namespaces on normal/abnormal exit, but `pkill -9` of the launcher can leak
them — the `ip -all netns delete` above scrubs anything left behind.

## Output

When the run finishes successfully:

```
montecarlo_results/parallel_slmode1_lunar_<TIMESTAMP>/
├── worker_0/
│   ├── worker.log
│   └── montecarlo_results.csv          # this worker's shard
├── worker_1/
│   └── ...
├── worker_2/
│   └── ...
├── worker_3/
│   └── ...
└── merged/
    ├── montecarlo_results.csv          # pooled CSV across all workers
    └── plots/                          # BLER waterfalls, auto-generated
```

If the auto-plot is skipped (`--no-plot`) or you want to re-plot manually:

```bash
LATEST=$(ls -td montecarlo_results/parallel_slmode1_lunar_* | head -1)
python3 plot_montecarlo.py "$LATEST/merged/montecarlo_results.csv" \
  --channel BICTR_LUNAR --direction DL \
  -o "$LATEST/merged/plots"
```

## Realistic wall-clock for 1000 × 1000

- ~7–8 MCS values per worker × 11 noise values × 1000 trials = 77,000 – 88,000
  trials per worker (max, before early-stop).
- Worst-case per-trial: 600 s timeout. Naïve worst case is therefore ~13,000
  hours per worker — completely impractical without early-stop.
- With `--early-stop 3`, most cells terminate in tens of seconds (saturated
  trivially). Only the waterfall-edge cells (typically 1–3 per MCS) need
  hundreds of trials.
- Realistic wall-clock on a 4-worker host with `--early-stop 3`: roughly
  **8–36 hours** end-to-end for the full BICTR_LUNAR sweep, depending on
  CPU and how wide the transition region is.

If you want a fast confidence check before committing to the full 1000×1000,
run the same command with `--trials 10 --target-tx 1000` first — that pass
takes ~1–3 hours on a 4-worker box and exercises every cell at least once.

## Running the same sweep inside Docker

The container image `oai-montecarlo:latest` (built from `Dockerfile.montecarlo`)
now supports the parallel sweep via a `--parallel` flag on
`docker-run-montecarlo.sh`. The wrapper auto-adds `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` and an
AppArmor opt-out in parallel mode (both needed for `ip netns add`).

Build once:

```bash
cd bictr_analysis
./docker-run-montecarlo.sh --build --parallel --workers 4 --trials 10 --target-tx 1000
```

Subsequent runs (no rebuild):

```bash
./docker-run-montecarlo.sh --parallel --workers 4 --trials 1000 --target-tx 1000 --warmup 15 --duration 600 --early-stop 3
```

What happens under the hood:

- The container runs as root (default `docker run` behavior).
- `iproute2` is preinstalled.
- The entrypoint pre-creates `/var/run/netns` so `ip netns add` works.
- Caps granted: `SYS_NICE`, `NET_ADMIN`, plus `SYS_ADMIN` only in `--parallel` mode.
- `/dev/net/tun` is mounted in; each per-worker netns gets its own
  `oaitun_enb1`/`oaitun_ue1`.
- `bictr_terrain/` is mounted read-only at the in-container path; results
  land in the host-bound `bictr_analysis/montecarlo_results/`.

Single-worker mode is unchanged (no `--parallel`): the wrapper keeps the
original minimal cap set (`SYS_NICE` + `NET_ADMIN`).

The `docker-export-montecarlo.sh` script now also bundles
`run_montecarlo_parallel_slmode1_lunar.sh`, `montecarlo_parallel_progress.py`,
and this `snapshot.readme` into the runtime tarball, so the parallel sweep
works out-of-the-box after `docker load` + `tar xzf` on a remote host.

## File map of the patches

- `run_montecarlo.sh`: sed-rewrites `rfsimulator.serverport` per worker; gNB
  CLI also receives `--rfsimulator.[0].serverport`. UE relies entirely on
  the conf (its CLI parser rejects the array-form key).
- `run_montecarlo_parallel_slmode1_lunar.sh`: creates `mc_worker_<TAG>_<i>`
  namespaces, brings `lo` up in each, wraps every `run_montecarlo.sh` worker
  invocation in `ip netns exec`, and tears the namespaces down on exit.
- `Dockerfile.montecarlo`: pre-creates `/var/run/netns` so the image is ready
  for `ip netns add` out of the box (`iproute2` was already installed).
- `scripts/docker-montecarlo-entry.sh`: idempotently `mkdir -p /var/run/netns`
  at container start (defensive for layered/overlay rootfs cases).
- `docker-run-montecarlo.sh`: new `--parallel` flag selects the parallel
  script and adds `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` + `--security-opt apparmor=unconfined`.
- `docker-export-montecarlo.sh`: now also packages the parallel script,
  progress helper, and this snapshot.readme into the runtime tarball.
